WEBVTT

00:00:00.601 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.637 --> 00:00:02.910
We have learned classic:

00:00:02.998 --> 00:00:05.630
one extension on each natural lash.

00:00:05.809 --> 00:00:06.670
Then volume:

00:00:07.011 --> 00:00:11.390
on each natural lash, a small fan of a few very fine lashes.

00:00:11.728 --> 00:00:14.190
Today it is hybrid, which means a mix.

00:00:14.572 --> 00:00:16.670
On the same eye, we combine both:

00:00:16.938 --> 00:00:19.390
a single extension here, a fan there.

00:00:19.754 --> 00:00:21.310
But one thing never changes:

00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:24.430
each natural lash carries exactly one thing.

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:26.510
Either a single, or a fan.

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:27.550
Never both.

00:00:28.186 --> 00:00:29.967
So what does hybrid look like?

00:00:30.471 --> 00:00:35.237
The singles are thicker and glossy black, standing out as distinct lashes,

00:00:35.187 --> 00:00:36.447
like little spikes.

00:00:37.032 --> 00:00:42.207
The fine fans fill the spaces in between, making the lash line full and soft.

00:00:42.636 --> 00:00:46.927
The result is a textured, fluffy, very natural lash line.

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:50.287
In the trade, it is often called a spiky look.

00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:55.407
It is fuller than classic, but softer and more natural than a full volume set.

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:57.340
Who does hybrid suit?

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:03.340
First, clients with sparse natural lashes, with gaps, or uneven lashes:

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.220
thick in some places, thin in others.

00:01:06.723 --> 00:01:11.268
Fine fans placed on the strong lashes around a gap make the lash line look full,

00:01:11.218 --> 00:01:13.740
without making weak lashes carry the weight.

00:01:14.218 --> 00:01:17.975
Next, clients used to classic, who now want a little more fullness,

00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:19.580
but are not ready for volume.

00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:21.580
Hybrid is the step in between.

00:01:21.895 --> 00:01:25.980
Many clients go from classic to hybrid, and only then to volume.

00:01:26.597 --> 00:01:29.189
This is the most important point of the lesson today.

00:01:29.691 --> 00:01:34.069
In hybrid, we do not choose singles or fans by a fixed pattern.

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:36.549
We choose for each natural lash.

00:01:36.916 --> 00:01:41.269
A strong, long, thick natural lash can carry a light fan.

00:01:41.696 --> 00:01:48.309
A fine, short lash, or a new baby lash, carries only a very fine, very short single.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.709
Some baby lashes are too weak, so leave them bare until the next refill.

00:01:52.952 --> 00:01:57.829
In other words, the strength of the natural lash decides, not a ratio on paper.

00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:01.038
So how many fans, and how many singles?

00:02:01.358 --> 00:02:02.638
People often say:

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.998
about half and half.

00:02:04.209 --> 00:02:07.278
Some say fans make up about 30 to 50 percent.

00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:09.918
Treat that as a starting point, not a rule.

00:02:10.243 --> 00:02:13.918
If the client has many strong lashes, you can use more fans.

00:02:14.185 --> 00:02:17.038
If her lashes are weak, use more light singles.

00:02:17.358 --> 00:02:20.478
The best number is the number her natural lashes can carry.

00:02:21.019 --> 00:02:23.854
Here is something that happens a lot with new technicians.

00:02:24.166 --> 00:02:25.534
They do hybrid in a rhythm:

00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:29.694
single, fan, single, fan, perfectly regular.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:30.974
It looks very neat.

00:02:31.379 --> 00:02:34.094
But that rhythm does not look at the natural lashes.

00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:36.746
So a weak baby lash ends up carrying a fan,

00:02:36.696 --> 00:02:39.934
while the strong lash next to it carries only a single.

00:02:40.043 --> 00:02:43.079
A few weeks later, those weak lashes fall out early,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:47.214
and the lash line thins out exactly where the client was already sparse.

00:02:47.386 --> 00:02:51.214
An even rhythm is good, but the rhythm must follow the natural lashes.

00:02:51.836 --> 00:02:53.458
Now let's talk about texture.

00:02:53.704 --> 00:02:56.738
Part of the texture of hybrid comes from how you mix the lengths.

00:02:56.903 --> 00:03:00.098
Some technicians make the singles slightly longer than the fans.

00:03:00.283 --> 00:03:05.298
The singles stick out above the fans as distinct spikes, for a sharper, bolder look.

00:03:05.807 --> 00:03:09.778
Other technicians make the singles the same length as the fans, or shorter.

00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:14.137
Then the fans sit on top, the lash line looks softer and fluffier,

00:03:14.087 --> 00:03:16.658
and the singles underneath give it depth.

00:03:16.922 --> 00:03:18.018
Both ways are correct.

00:03:18.433 --> 00:03:21.378
Which one you choose depends on the look you agreed with the client.

00:03:21.807 --> 00:03:23.058
Keep the difference small.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.578
Too big, and the lash line looks messy and careless.

00:03:27.257 --> 00:03:32.354
In a beautiful hybrid set, fans and singles are spread evenly across the lash line.

00:03:32.927 --> 00:03:34.914
Never bunch the fans in one spot.

00:03:35.419 --> 00:03:37.696
If all the fans are bunched in one place,

00:03:37.646 --> 00:03:41.554
and elsewhere there are only a few singles, the lash line looks patchy:

00:03:41.842 --> 00:03:44.914
dark and heavy in one place, sparse in another.

00:03:45.423 --> 00:03:49.140
To avoid this, work zone by zone, and after each zone,

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.314
step back and look at the whole.

00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:53.234
Both eyes must match, too.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:58.204
The safety rules are exactly the same as in the classic and volume lessons.

00:03:58.712 --> 00:04:04.284
Each single or each fan goes on exactly one natural lash, isolated cleanly.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:05.324
No stickies.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:11.004
Attach about 0.5 to 1 mm from the eyelid skin, never touching the skin.

00:04:11.513 --> 00:04:13.324
And keep the glue drop very small.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:17.490
With hybrid, your hands keep switching between singles and fans,

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.084
so it is very easy to rush.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.084
Keep your hands slow and steady.

00:04:21.722 --> 00:04:24.120
Natural lashes shed with their life cycle,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:28.537
so the client needs to come back for refills, usually after two to three weeks,

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.417
as you have learned.

00:04:29.812 --> 00:04:33.737
At a refill, never just redo exactly what you did last time.

00:04:34.163 --> 00:04:35.817
Read the natural lashes again.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:40.198
A baby lash you left bare last time, or gave only a fine single,

00:04:40.148 --> 00:04:42.297
may now be strong enough for a fan.

00:04:42.642 --> 00:04:46.147
And remind the client to look after her lashes properly at home,

00:04:46.097 --> 00:04:47.497
as in the classic lesson.

00:04:48.151 --> 00:04:51.513
Finally, consult carefully and be honest with the client.

00:04:51.893 --> 00:04:54.473
Show her hybrid photos, and make it clear:

00:04:54.823 --> 00:04:59.753
this is a fluffy, textured look, not a solid black lash line like volume.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.713
If her lashes are sparse, say gently:

00:05:03.142 --> 00:05:07.513
this time, we will use more singles, so your natural lashes stay healthy.

00:05:08.077 --> 00:05:12.233
When she understands beforehand, she is not surprised when she opens her eyes.

00:05:12.404 --> 00:05:14.633
And when she trusts you, she comes back.

00:05:15.266 --> 00:05:15.994
So you see.

00:05:16.245 --> 00:05:18.954
Hybrid is not hard because you do two techniques.

00:05:19.298 --> 00:05:23.034
It is hard because every time you attach, you have to ask yourself:

00:05:23.276 --> 00:05:25.434
what can this natural lash carry?

00:05:25.906 --> 00:05:30.954
Answer that question correctly, and the set will be natural, even, and long lasting.

00:05:31.209 --> 00:05:34.634
In the practice lesson, we will do a hybrid set step by step.

00:05:34.903 --> 00:05:37.514
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:37.614 --> 00:05:38.474
See you next time.
